# Dormant iPhone host-compatibility baseline.
# Public-source cleanup generalized one operator-identifying AppDelegate comment;
# executable host-compatibility code and behavior are unchanged.
#
# Reference inspection: Wispr Flow 1.71/build 1698, ChatGPT 1.2026.224,
# and Claude 1.260820.0 on 2026-08-23. Automatic return was explicitly retired
# on 2026-08-24. These files stay pinned so dormant compatibility evidence is
# not casually rewritten or reconnected. See ios-keyboard-roundtrip-spec.md.
# The 2026-08-24 Expo migration changed only the containing-app entry and
# required Expo plist keys; the dormant host resolution below it was audited
# unchanged before this baseline was advanced.
# The 2026-08-24 live-cursor delivery decision removed only the active
# fingerprint veto from SharedDictation and KeyboardModel. Dormant host capture,
# resolution, catalog, and return code remain disconnected and unchanged.
# The 2026-08-25 delivery reliability update changed the containing-app plist
# only to follow the system appearance, and changed the active keyboard path to
# wait for an attached document proxy, confirm the current-proxy mutation, and
# retain/report unconfirmed delivery. Dormant host capture, resolution, catalog,
# and return code remain disconnected and unchanged.
# The explicit 2026-08-27 dual-channel decision changed SharedDictation and
# KeyboardModel so a realtime draft and the quality-first batch result arbitrate
# one insertion under the existing lock. It did not reconnect dormant host
# capture, resolution, catalog, or automatic return.
# The explicit 2026-08-27 Control Center state-machine decision added shared
# Pausing and Resuming phases plus matching optimistic keyboard presentation.
# It did not reconnect dormant host capture, resolution, catalog, or return.
# The explicit 2026-08-28 Dictation Button rebrand changed only display copy in
# the containing-app plist, shared delivery warning, and keyboard model. Internal
# identifiers and dormant host capture, resolution, catalog, and return remain
# The authorized 2026-09-08 public-review preparation removes the bundled
# provider credential from app launch/plist and adds local character editing
# plus an always-visible keyboard switch. Dormant host-resolution, capture,
# catalog, and automatic-return source remains unchanged and is excluded
# from the public keyboard target. The shipping controller now uses public
# document-proxy/lifecycle APIs and requires the user to return manually.
# unchanged and disconnected.
